cmu-industry-source-hand = Hand crafting
cmu-industry-source-hand-help = Carry the materials and tools. Right-click yourself → Craft, then choose this recipe.
cmu-industry-source-machine = Machine
cmu-industry-source-machine-help = Use one of the listed machines. Supply power (or steam for a steam model), load the inputs and leave output space. Pipe fluids into the matching INPUT ports and collect them from OUTPUT ports.
cmu-industry-source-assembly = Blueprint assembly
cmu-industry-source-assembly-help = Activate a blueprint in hand and program this recipe. Insert it and a charged cell into the assembly machine. Fill the numbered material slots as listed for ONE batch, leaving other slots empty. Collect the output and reload for the next batch.
cmu-industry-source-assembly-slot = Slot {$slot}: {$count} × {$name}
cmu-industry-source-grinder = Grinding
cmu-industry-source-grinder-help = Load the material into a powered grinder, or supply steam to a steam grinder. Collect all products from its output slots.
cmu-industry-source-crush = Hammer crushing
cmu-industry-source-crush-help = Hold a hammer and click the loose material. Hand crushing gives less powder than a grinder; the quantities here already show that reduction.
cmu-industry-source-alloy = Electric smelting
cmu-industry-source-alloy-help = Power the smelter, load the listed materials and set the temperature high enough. Leave its output slot free.
cmu-industry-source-press = Pressing
cmu-industry-source-press-help = Load the inputs into a press. Put the listed mold in its mold slot; leave that slot empty when no mold is listed. Fuel a solid-fuel press with planks, or connect steam to a steam press. Supply any listed fluids and collect the output.
cmu-industry-source-steam = Steam smelting
cmu-industry-source-steam-help = Supply steam, load the materials and put the mold in its mold slot. Open the steam regulator. Drain slag from models that produce it; a full slag tank stops work.
cmu-industry-source-condenser = Condensing
cmu-industry-source-condenser-help = Pipe the liquid and coolant into their matching INPUT ports, load any listed solid material, and leave the output slot free. Power an electric condenser; a brass condenser needs a steady coolant reserve instead.
cmu-industry-source-anvil = Anvil forging
cmu-industry-source-anvil-help = Heat the workpiece in a fueled furnace. Use tongs to seat it on the anvil, then click it with a hammer or chisel to choose this recipe. Follow the tool order and reheat when too cold.
cmu-industry-source-cast = Casting
cmu-industry-source-cast-help = Use tongs to pour the molten contents of a crucible into this casting mold. Let it cool, then right-click the mold → Extract casting. Click each liquid below to see how to melt it.
cmu-industry-source-melt = Crucible melting
cmu-industry-source-melt-help = Click a crucible with the material to load it. Use tongs to place it in a fueled, lit furnace; heat it to the required temperature. Lift it with tongs and pour into a casting mold. Iron needs the hotter stone furnace.
cmu-industry-source-pot = Smelting pot
cmu-industry-source-pot-help = Load one material type into the pot, then place it on a lit campfire. Let the batch finish and collect the output before loading another material.
cmu-industry-source-mine = Mining drop
cmu-industry-source-mine-help = Mine the listed wall or vein underground. Use a shovel for clay, a pickaxe for stone, or a charged jackhammer for black rock. This is a possible drop; deposits, veins and yields vary by location and cavern generation.
cmu-industry-source-drill = Drilling
cmu-industry-source-drill-help = Find the listed deposit underground (a powered prospector helps). Place a drill over it, provide electricity or steam to suit the drill, and collect ore from its output slots. A deposit contains only some of the ores in its source table.
cmu-industry-source-rock-help = Place the drill on the matching stone or black-rock cave floor. Supply electricity or steam for that drill and collect rock from its output slots; no ore deposit is needed for ordinary rock.
cmu-industry-source-chop = Woodcutting
cmu-industry-source-chop-help = Fell the listed tree with an axe, then pick up the dropped logs. Use a hand saw on a log for planks. Logs require both hands to carry.
cmu-industry-source-firewood-help = Strike this tree with an axe to knock off firewood. Each tree has a limited supply; logs can also be split for more.
cmu-industry-source-split-help = Click the log with an axe to split it into firewood. Use a hand saw instead if you want planks.
cmu-industry-source-refine = Tool processing
cmu-industry-source-extract = Reagent grinding
cmu-industry-source-extract-help = Insert a beaker and the input item into a reagent grinder. Choose Grind, then collect the beaker. These are the item's starting contents; used or grown items may yield different amounts.
cmu-industry-source-juice = Juicing
cmu-industry-source-juice-help = Insert a beaker and the input item into a reagent grinder. Choose Juice, then collect the beaker. The listed liquids are the juice products, not the Grind products.
cmu-industry-source-refine-help = Hold the listed tool and use it on the input item. Wait for the action to finish, then pick up the products. Possible or variable drops have no fixed quantity shown.
cmu-industry-source-butcher-help = Hold a suitable knife and right-click the carcass → Butcher. Wait until it can no longer be revived if required. Collect the products afterward; hides and other chance drops are not guaranteed.
cmu-industry-source-gather = Gathering
cmu-industry-source-gather-help = Find this plant and use a suitable harvesting tool on it. Cut high bushes with a knife for plant fiber. Harvests can depend on the tool and growth stage; the listed product is a possible drop.
cmu-industry-source-branch-help = Right-click the tree → Break off a branch. Branches regrow after a delay; you can also craft branches from planks.
cmu-industry-source-resin-help = Use a knife on the tree to open its bark, then use a reagent container on it to collect resin. The hole closes and the tree needs time to replenish its resin.
cmu-industry-source-pump = Pumping
cmu-industry-source-oil-help = Find an oil deposit underground with a powered prospector. Place this pump on the deposit, supply electricity, and connect its OUTPUT to touching fluid pipes leading to storage or processing.
cmu-industry-source-water-help = Place this pump directly on water, such as shallow water or a cave pool. Connect its OUTPUT to touching fluid pipes leading to a tank or machine. Dry ground supplies no water.
cmu-industry-source-unknown = Other acquisition
cmu-industry-source-unknown-help = No production or gathering source is recorded for this item in the industry finder. Check its right-click Help entry for other ways to obtain or use it.
